# Deliberate, reviewed exceptions — mirrors the raw manifests in AstroLumina-Kubernetes:
#   KSV-0014: the frontend container keeps a writable root filesystem because its
#   entrypoint rewrites /usr/share/nginx/html/{env.js,index.html} with sed -i at
#   container start. The three API containers DO set readOnlyRootFilesystem: true —
#   do not weaken them. The same gap is tracked as an advisory finding in the
#   Kubernetes repo (see its trivy-config step comment and .kube-linter.yaml).
KSV-0014

# Bare-render-only artifact: the CI scan renders the chart with NO -f values file,
# so services render without pinned image tags. Every real environment pins tags
# via values-<env>.yaml (imageTags per service/color).
KSV-0013

# The images come from our own org registry (ghcr.io/astrolumina-rise-n-shine/*);
# ghcr.io is simply not on the check's built-in trusted-registry list.
KSV-0125

# Deliberate project-wide choice: containers run as UID/GID 1001 (frontend 101),
# matching the raw manifests and Dockerfiles — far below the check's preferred
# > 10000. Tracked as an advisory gap in the Kubernetes repo too (same UID/GID).
KSV-0020
KSV-0021
